SUMMARY:Make & Take: Sourdough Bread for Beginners
DESCRIPTION:Join us if you love to bake! \nIn recent years\, it seems everybody’s been talking about sourdough. Still\, this delicious bread is a bit of a mystery to many. If you’re curious about sourdough\, join us for this hour-long class. Amelia Detwiler of Willow House Goods will talk about how sourdough is different from other types of breads\, and she’ll demonstrate the care and feeding of sourdough starter and discuss the basics of the first bake. \nEach guest will go home with a Sourdough Starter Kit that includes everything they need to start baking immediately: \n\n1 jar of active\, hydrated\, ready-to use sourdough starter\nA professional-grade class fermentation jar that they can use to hold and maintain their starter\nA traditional wooden spurtle to stir deep into the jar for a perfect mix with less mess\nA stylish breathable cotton bonnet for the jar\nProfessional instruction sheets\, including step-by-step feeding guides and schedule\, a beginner-friendly recipe\, and trouble-shooting tips\n\nSourdough has prebiotics\, or healthy gut bacteria. It also has less gluten and a lower glycemic index than some other breads. \nTwo sessions are available\, starting at 10 a.m. or 1 p.m. Walk-ins are welcome if space is available\, but reservations are strongly recommended. \n$65 per person includes instruction and Sourdough Starter Kit. \nDate: Saturday\, November 14 \nTimes: 10 a.m. and 1 p.m. \nTo save your space: Call (717) 344-6875. Reservations strongly recommended.
URL:https://bird-in-hand.com/event/make-take-sourdough-bread-for-beginners-2/
LOCATION:Bird-in-Hand Artisan Village\, 2705 Old Philadelphia Pike\, Bird-in-Hand\, PA\, 17505\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bird-in-hand.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/SourdoughClass_Web.jpg
END:VEVENT
